From 2a122f01ffe10a7ce478cb2881ab552fc3acdd27 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-v13 <v13@localhost>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 07:37:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] codegen: fold constant copies straight into the
 destination register

emit_copy_value relayed every constant copy through %rax: 'movq $imm, %rax;
movq %rax, %reg'. The short-circuit merge value (x = 1) and loop preambles pay
this relay per execution; emit the constant directly (movq $imm, %reg / xorl
for zero) via operand_to_callee_reg, which already special-cases every integer
constant form. Slot/accumulator-sourced copies keep the %rax relay (their
width-aware load semantics must be preserved). Verified in Expat's nameLength
hot path: 'mov $0x1,%rax; mov %rax,%rbp' -> 'mov $0x1,%rbp' (4x per scanned
character).

New regression tests: bool_return_materialization (short-circuit return-bool
materialization across inlining boundaries) and fp_param_wide (8-F64/5-F32
parameter lists exercising the FP-param pre-store ordering + scratch cycle
break).
---
 src/backend/x86/codegen/emit.rs               | 16 +++++--
 .../regression/bool_return_materialization.c  | 48 +++++++++++++++++++
 tests/regression/fp_param_wide.c              | 45 +++++++++++++++++
 tests/regression/fp_param_wide.flags          |  1 +
 4 files changed, 107 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/regression/bool_return_materialization.c
 create mode 100644 tests/regression/fp_param_wide.c
 create mode 100644 tests/regression/fp_param_wide.flags

